    "Period is a subdivision of an era, typically lasting tens of millions of years.",
    "An example of a period is the Jurassic Period, which lasted from 201 to 145 million years.",
    "Epoch is a subdivision of a period, typically lasting millions of years.",
    "An example of an epoch is the Early Jurassic Epoch, which lasted from 201 to 175 million years.",
    "Age is a subdivision of an epoch, typically lasting hundreds of thousands to millions of years.",
    "An example of an age is the Pliensbachian Age, which lasted from 190 to 184 million years.",
    "The division basis for these units is based on significant geologic events.",
    "Significant geologic events include changes in sea level, tectonic activity, or major faunal turnovers.",
    "Boundaries between units are established by the International Commission on Stratigraphy (ICS)."
